---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
import { dataHub } from "../data/members";
import { a0 } from "../data/a0_results";

const k = (x: number) => Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en-AU");
const pct = Math.round(a0.loss_reduction_vs_naive_pct);
const t2 = (kg: number) => (kg / 1000).toFixed(2);
const principles = [
  { h: "One result format", p: "Every package writes its result in the same structure, so the next package can check it and use it directly." },
  { h: "Declining to answer", p: "A package that cannot answer soundly says so, with its reason, in the same format. Later packages carry that forward instead of guessing." },
  { h: "conductoR runs the plan", p: "An analysis plan is a list of steps, each done by one package. conductoR runs them in order and stops if a result is the wrong kind for the next step." },
  { h: "Open data in the orchestra", p: `DataHub holds ${dataHub.nDatasets} open datasets, ${dataHub.nAustralia} of them Australian, each with its source and licence, and finds the datasets that can answer a given question.` },
];
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite",
  name: site.name, description: site.intro,
  author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Max Moldovan", identifier: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9680-8474" },
};
---
<Base title="Home" description={site.intro} path="/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-in">
      <p class="kicker">Crop analytics · {site.counts.members} R packages and a data catalogue</p>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">Crop Analytics Orchestra</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-3">Crop analytics usually joins separate tools by hand, one analysis
        at a time. These {site.counts.members} R packages and an open data catalogue, DataHub, are
        built to work together. Each does one job well on its own, all return results in one shared
        format, and each can decline to answer when the data cannot support an answer.</p>
      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href={href("/members")}>Explore the packages</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/a0")}>See the study</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">How the packages work together</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid four">
      {principles.map((x) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{x.h}</h3>
          <p class="muted mt-2">{x.p}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">One nitrogen decision</p>
      <h2>{pct}% less money lost than trusting the crop simulator alone</h2>
      <p class="prose muted mt-2">On a synthetic barley belt built on real climate and soil
        records at {a0.n_sites} sites, the full chain of packages chose nitrogen rates site by
        site. Where the field record disagreed with the simulator, the chain stopped using the
        simulator and fitted the field data instead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-stats">
      <div class="hs"><span class="n">{k(a0.loss_cascade_total_aud_ha)}</span><span class="l">AUD/ha lost, orchestra</span></div>
      <div class="hs"><span class="n">{k(a0.loss_naive_total_aud_ha)}</span><span class="l">AUD/ha lost, simulator alone</span></div>
      <div class="hs"><span class="n">{k(a0.n_saved_vs_naive_kgn)}</span><span class="l">kg N not applied</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="prose muted mt-3">Cause and effect: in farm-style records drawn from the same plots, where
      wetter sites get more nitrogen, a naive reading puts the gain from 150 kg N/ha at{" "}
      {t2(a0.causal_naive_150)} t/ha against a planted {t2(a0.causal_truth_150)}. Adjusting for rainfall
      gives {t2(a0.causal_backdoor_150)} t/ha (medians of {a0.causal_n_samples} samples).</p>
    <p class="prose muted small mt-3">The belt is synthetic: the numbers show the method at
      work, not what a real paddock would earn.</p>
    <p class="cta-row"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/a0")}>The study, step by step</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .four { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) { .four { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
